# bat config. "ansi" is bat's built-in 16-color theme: it maps syntax tokens
# onto the terminal's ANSI slots (gruvbox dark hard), so `cat`/`bat` (and
# anything reading this config) follows the terminal palette instead of a pinned
# one. Matches the television previews, which already force BAT_THEME=ansi.
--theme="ansi"
--style="numbers,changes,header"
--paging=auto
